; Executed-code gate for THE PICTURE THAT OUTLIVES THE PAYLOAD.
;
; THE RULING THIS EXISTS UNDER, 2026-09-11: a payload ran four times, came
; back clean every time and put nothing on the panel; the fifth drew a
; garbled frame, and nothing in any of those five transcripts could tell the
; five runs apart. Every board run comes back with a picture now.
;
; WHAT IS ACTUALLY EXECUTED HERE is the SHIPPED bodies - ScrCaptureToArea,
; ScrCaptureSnapshot and the three readers from screen_source.pi4, ScrShotTier
; and ScrShotNow from screen_cmd.pi4, the rotation map from screen_geom.pi4,
; the whole of RunAt from cache.pi4, and Anvil/Core/shotarm.pbi as included
; rather than modelled. Every leaf is a stub that COUNTS or RECORDS. There is
; no hardware, no panel, no mailbox and no GPU.
;
; THE TWO THINGS THIS GATE IS FOR, and both are invisible on a quiet bench:
;
;   1. THE CAPTURE IS OF THE PRESENTED PHYSICAL FRAME. With the console
;      sideways the bytes the console draws into are NOT the bytes the panel
;      scans, and a capture of the drawing buffer is a picture of an
;      intention. The modelled panel below is deliberately turned, and the
;      two buffers deliberately hold different pixels, so capturing the
;      wrong one cannot pass.
;
;   2. IT HAPPENS BEFORE THE REPAINT. The monitor's own report that a
;      payload returned is printed through the console grid onto the
;      surface being asked about, so on the board that printing IS the
;      repaint. The printing stubs here look at the capture area at the
;      FIRST character printed after the payload came back: if the magic
;      is not there yet, the frame was painted over before it was kept.
;
; #MON_FB_PANEL_W/H and the capture area are MODELLED SMALL so the whole
; thing runs in a few hundred thousand emitted instructions. The real
; addresses and sizes in RaspberryPi4/Board/memmap.pi4 are checked
; statically by tools/screen_shot_emitted_check.py, which is the right
; layer for "is this region clear of every other owner" - that is a question
; about a list, not about a copy loop.

; THE ARM'S OWN GLOBALS. Anvil/Core/shotarm.pbi is not included here: its
; five procedure bodies are SPLICED in with the rest of the product, so that
; a mutant can be made of them too - the one-shot arm is a rule about
; ordering and a gate that could not mutate it would only be asserting that
; today's code does what today's code does.
Global gShotArm.i
#DSP_DMA_LINKED = 1
Global gate_quarantined.i
Global gate_mirrorOff.i
Global gate_rendererOff.i
Procedure UartMirror(on.i)
  If on=0 : gate_mirrorOff=gate_mirrorOff+1 : EndIf
EndProcedure
Procedure ConNoRenderer()
  gate_rendererOff=gate_rendererOff+1
EndProcedure
Procedure.i DmaQuarantined()
  ProcedureReturn gate_quarantined
EndProcedure
Procedure.i CoreAcceptOwnsSecondaries()
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure
Procedure.i CoreAcceptReclaim()
  ProcedureReturn 1
EndProcedure
Global gShotSeq.i

; ---- the vocabulary the product files use ----------------------------
#SCR_SRC_NONE = 0
#SCR_SRC_HDMI = 1
#SCR_SRC_DSI  = 2
#HW_TIER_CPU  = 0
#HW_TIER_DMA  = 1
#HW_TIER_V3D  = 2
#ANVIL_V3D_CONSOLE = 1

; ---- the modelled panel: 8 across, 12 down, portrait ------------------
#MON_FB_PANEL_W = 8
#MON_FB_PANEL_H = 12
#MON_FB_SCAN    = $07000000     ; what the panel scans
#MON_FB_DRAW    = $07010000     ; what a sideways console draws into

; ---- the modelled capture area ----------------------------------------
; The pixel window is deliberately tight: 4096 bytes holds the modelled
; panel's 384 and refuses the oversized HDMI surface below, which is how
; the refusal path gets executed rather than reasoned about.
#MON_SHOT_HDR       = $07100000
#MON_SHOT_PIX       = $07101000
#MON_SHOT_PIX_BYTES = 4096
#MON_SHOT_MAGIC     = $414E5653484F5431
#MON_SHOT_OFF_MAGIC  = 0
#MON_SHOT_OFF_SEQ    = 8
#MON_SHOT_OFF_W      = 16
#MON_SHOT_OFF_H      = 24
#MON_SHOT_OFF_PITCH  = 32
#MON_SHOT_OFF_ROT    = 40
#MON_SHOT_OFF_TIER   = 48
#MON_SHOT_OFF_X0     = 56
#MON_SHOT_OFF_PANELW = 64
#MON_SHOT_OFF_PANELH = 72
#MON_SHOT_OFF_BPP    = 80
#MON_SHOT_OFF_SRC    = 88
#MON_SHOT_OFF_WHO    = 96
#MON_SHOT_OFF_BYTES  = 104
#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD = 0
#MON_SHOT_WHO_RETURN  = 1

; where this gate writes its answers for the host to read
#GATE_OUT = $07200000

; ---- the state the product reads -------------------------------------
Global gScrSrc.i
Global gScrRot.i
Global gScrDsiUp.i
Global gDma.i
Global gV3dConOn.i

; the HDMI surface the firmware would have handed over
Global gate_hdmiBase.i
Global gate_hdmiW.i
Global gate_hdmiH.i
Global gate_hdmiPitch.i
Global gate_hdmiBpp.i

; what the stubs saw
Global gate_paints.i           ; every printing primitive the product reached
Global gate_afterCall.i        ; 1 once the modelled payload has returned
Global gate_paintsAfter.i      ; printing done AFTER the payload returned
Global gate_magicAtFirstPaint.i ; was a picture already kept by then?
Global gate_drain.i
Global gate_ethQuiesce.i
Global gate_ethReclaim.i
Global gate_ethResume.i
Global gate_kbdSuspend.i
Global gate_kbdResume.i
Global gate_cacheOff.i
Global gate_cacheOn.i
Global gate_wdStart.i
Global gate_wdStop.i
Global gate_recEnter.i
Global gate_recReturn.i
Global gate_recOrder.i
Global gate_calls.i
Global gate_firmware.i
Global gate_dhcpTicks.i
Global gate_rearms.i
Global gate_dmaResets.i
Global gate_hitsMonitor.i

Global gDead.i
Global gCacheOn.i
Global gGoAddr.i
Global gGoRc.i
Global gGoX0.i
Global gMonHitLo.i
Global gMonHitHi.i
Global gsp.i
Global gate_payloadRc.i        ; what the modelled payload "returns"
Global gate_hitsAnswer.i       ; what HitsMonitor is to say this time

; ======================================================================
;  THE LEAVES. Every one counts or records; none touches hardware.
;
;  PRINTING IS OBSERVED AT THE PRIMITIVES AND NOT AT Print ITSELF, because
;  Print and PrintN are statements in this language rather than procedures:
;  the compiler routes a literal to str_print_at, a number to PrintDec and
;  the line ending to PrintNl. Stubbing those three is stubbing every way
;  the monitor can put a character on its console.
;
;  AND THE STUB IS WHERE THE ORDERING IS MEASURED. On the real board a
;  printed line IS the repaint - it goes through the console grid onto the
;  surface being asked about - so "was the frame kept before anything
;  repainted over it" is answered by asking, at the FIRST print after the
;  payload came back, whether the capture area already holds a picture.
;  Nothing in the capture path prints, so there is no interference.
; ======================================================================
Procedure gate_paint()
  gate_paints = gate_paints + 1
  If gate_afterCall <> 0
    gate_paintsAfter = gate_paintsAfter + 1
    If gate_magicAtFirstPaint = -1
      gate_magicAtFirstPaint = PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_MAGIC)
    EndIf
  EndIf
EndProcedure

Procedure str_print_at(p.i) : gate_paint() : EndProcedure
Procedure UartWriteStr(s.i) : gate_paint() : EndProcedure
Procedure PrintDec(v.i)     : gate_paint() : EndProcedure
Procedure PrintNl()         : gate_paint() : EndProcedure
Procedure PutAddr(a.i)      : gate_paint() : EndProcedure
Procedure PutHex16(v.i)     : gate_paint() : EndProcedure
Procedure UartDrain()       : gate_drain = gate_drain + 1 : EndProcedure
Procedure NetConsoleFlush() : EndProcedure
Procedure NetConsoleRearm() : gate_rearms = gate_rearms + 1 : EndProcedure
Procedure NetDhcpTick()    : gate_dhcpTicks = gate_dhcpTicks + 1 : EndProcedure
Procedure TouchKeyboardPayloadSuspend() : gate_kbdSuspend = gate_kbdSuspend + 1 : EndProcedure
Procedure TouchKeyboardPayloadResume()  : gate_kbdResume = gate_kbdResume + 1 : EndProcedure
Procedure.i EthPayloadQuiesce() : gate_ethQuiesce = gate_ethQuiesce + 1 : ProcedureReturn 0 : EndProcedure
Procedure.i EthPayloadReclaim() : gate_ethReclaim = gate_ethReclaim + 1 : ProcedureReturn 1 : EndProcedure
Procedure.i EthPayloadResume(was.i) : gate_ethResume = gate_ethResume + 1 : ProcedureReturn 0 : EndProcedure
Procedure EthWhyGenet()    : EndProcedure
Procedure SafetyToFirmware() : gate_firmware = gate_firmware + 1 : EndProcedure
Procedure.i SafetyWatchdogStart(s.i) : gate_wdStart = gate_wdStart + 1 : ProcedureReturn s : EndProcedure
Procedure SafetyWatchdogStop() : gate_wdStop = gate_wdStop + 1 : EndProcedure
; The run record (RaspberryPi4/Board/runrecord.pi4) has its own executed gate;
; here only WHERE RunAt writes it is checked: entry after every refusal and
; directly before the jump, return directly after it and before the picture.
Procedure RunRecordEnter(a.i, d.i)
  gate_recEnter = gate_recEnter + 1
  gate_recOrder = gate_calls
EndProcedure
Procedure RunRecordReturn(x0.i)
  gate_recReturn = gate_recReturn + 1
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_MAGIC) = #MON_SHOT_MAGIC
    gate_recOrder = -1
  EndIf
EndProcedure
Procedure CacheDisable()   : gate_cacheOff = gate_cacheOff + 1 : EndProcedure
Procedure CacheEnable()    : gate_cacheOn = gate_cacheOn + 1 : EndProcedure
Procedure.i DmaChannelReset() : gate_dmaResets = gate_dmaResets + 1 : ProcedureReturn 1 : EndProcedure
Procedure.i DisplayUseDma(on.i) : ProcedureReturn 1 : EndProcedure
Procedure.i HitsMonitor(lo.i, hi.i)
  gate_hitsMonitor = gate_hitsMonitor + 1
  ProcedureReturn gate_hitsAnswer
EndProcedure

; THE PAYLOAD ITSELF. CallAddr in the product is inline assembly that
; branches into the payload and stores x0 into gGoRc on the way back. The
; modelled version does exactly what matters to this gate: it hands the
; return value over in the same global, in the same place, and it opens the
; window in which the ordering above is being watched.
Procedure CallAddr()
  gate_calls = gate_calls + 1
  gGoRc = gate_payloadRc
  gate_afterCall = 1
  gate_paintsAfter = 0
  gate_magicAtFirstPaint = -1
EndProcedure

; The HDMI half of the snapshot seam.
Procedure.i DisplayViewBase()       : ProcedureReturn gate_hdmiBase  : EndProcedure
Procedure.i DisplayWidth()          : ProcedureReturn gate_hdmiW     : EndProcedure
Procedure.i DisplayHeight()         : ProcedureReturn gate_hdmiH     : EndProcedure
Procedure.i DisplayPitch()          : ProcedureReturn gate_hdmiPitch : EndProcedure
Procedure.i DisplayBytesPerPixel()  : ProcedureReturn gate_hdmiBpp   : EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  THE SHIPPED BODIES GO HERE. tools/screen_shot_emitted_check.py splices
;  them in at this marker, straight out of the product files.
; ======================================================================
; @@BODY@@

; ======================================================================
;  THE MODELLED SCREEN. Two buffers with DIFFERENT contents, so a capture
;  of the wrong one cannot look like a capture of the right one.
; ======================================================================
Procedure gate_fill(base.i, w.i, h.i, tag.i)
  Define x.i
  Define y.i
  y = 0
  While y < h
    x = 0
    While x < w
      PokeL(base + y * w * 4 + x * 4, $FF000000 | (tag << 16) | (y << 8) | x)
      x = x + 1
    Wend
    y = y + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

Procedure gate_wipeArea()
  Define i.i
  i = 0
  While i < 128
    PokeI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + i, 0)
    i = i + 8
  Wend
  i = 0
  While i < #MON_SHOT_PIX_BYTES
    PokeI(#MON_SHOT_PIX + i, 0)
    i = i + 8
  Wend
EndProcedure

; 1 when the captured pixels are the SCAN buffer byte for byte.
Procedure.i gate_copyIsScan(n.i)
  Define i.i
  i = 0
  While i < n
    If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_PIX + i) <> PeekI(#MON_FB_SCAN + i)
      ProcedureReturn 0
    EndIf
    i = i + 8
  Wend
  ProcedureReturn 1
EndProcedure

Procedure.i gate_copyIsDraw(n.i)
  Define i.i
  i = 0
  While i < n
    If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_PIX + i) <> PeekI(#MON_FB_DRAW + i)
      ProcedureReturn 0
    EndIf
    i = i + 8
  Wend
  ProcedureReturn 1
EndProcedure

Procedure gate_fresh()
  gate_quarantined = 0
  gate_paints = 0
  gate_afterCall = 0
  gate_paintsAfter = 0
  gate_magicAtFirstPaint = -1
  gate_hitsAnswer = 0
  gate_drain = 0
  gate_ethQuiesce = 0
  gate_ethReclaim = 0
  gate_ethResume = 0
  gate_kbdSuspend = 0
  gate_kbdResume = 0
  gate_cacheOff = 0
  gate_cacheOn = 0
  gate_wdStart = 0
  gate_wdStop = 0
  gate_recEnter = 0
  gate_recReturn = 0
  gate_recOrder = 0
  gate_calls = 0
  gate_firmware = 0
  gate_dhcpTicks = 0
  gate_rearms = 0
  gate_dmaResets = 0
  gate_hitsMonitor = 0
  gate_wipeArea()
  ; The two buffers, with different tags. 8 x 12 physical and 12 x 8
  ; logical are the same 96 pixels, so a wrong-buffer capture is the same
  ; LENGTH and different BYTES - which is the only shape of this bug that
  ; ever reaches a panel.
  gate_fill(#MON_FB_SCAN, #MON_FB_PANEL_W, #MON_FB_PANEL_H, $11)
  gate_fill(#MON_FB_DRAW, #MON_FB_PANEL_H, #MON_FB_PANEL_W, $22)
EndProcedure

; Every header word, checked against what the modelled screen was. Answers
; 0 when they all agree, or the offset of the first that did not, so a
; failure names the field.
Procedure.i gate_header(w.i, h.i, pitch.i, rot.i, tier.i, x0.i, pw.i, ph.i, src.i, who.i, nbytes.i, seq.i)
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_MAGIC) <> #MON_SHOT_MAGIC : ProcedureReturn 1 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_SEQ) <> seq : ProcedureReturn 2 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_W) <> w : ProcedureReturn 3 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_H) <> h : ProcedureReturn 4 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_PITCH) <> pitch : ProcedureReturn 5 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_ROT) <> rot : ProcedureReturn 6 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_TIER) <> tier : ProcedureReturn 7 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_X0) <> x0 : ProcedureReturn 8 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_PANELW) <> pw : ProcedureReturn 9 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_PANELH) <> ph : ProcedureReturn 10 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_BPP) <> 4 : ProcedureReturn 11 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_SRC) <> src : ProcedureReturn 12 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_WHO) <> who : ProcedureReturn 13 : EndIf
  If PeekI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_BYTES) <> nbytes : ProcedureReturn 14 : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  THE GATE
; ======================================================================
Procedure.i Main()
  Define rc.i
  Define x.i
  Define y.i
  Define live.i
  Define kept.i

  gShotArm = 0
  gShotSeq = 0
  gMonHitLo = $00200000
  gMonHitHi = $004FFFFF

  ; ---- 1. THE TURNED PANEL, FRAMEBUFFER TIER. The whole feature in one
  ;         assertion: the copy is the scan buffer and NOT the drawing one.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_DSI
  gScrRot = 90
  gScrDsiUp = 1
  gDma = 1
  gV3dConOn = 0
  If ScrShotNow(#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 0) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 10 : EndIf
  rc = gate_header(12, 8, 32, 90, #HW_TIER_DMA, 0, 8, 12, #SCR_SRC_DSI, #MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 384, 1)
  If rc <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 20 + rc : EndIf
  If gate_copyIsScan(384) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 11 : EndIf
  ; AND IT IS NOT THE DRAWING BUFFER. Said as its own assertion rather than
  ; implied by the one above, because the two buffers are the same size and
  ; a mutant that copies the wrong one passes every length check there is.
  If gate_copyIsDraw(384) <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 12 : EndIf
  If ScrShotValid() <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 13 : EndIf
  If ScrShotPixels() <> #MON_SHOT_PIX : ProcedureReturn 14 : EndIf
  If ScrShotField(#MON_SHOT_OFF_ROT) <> 90 : ProcedureReturn 15 : EndIf

  ; ---- 2. THE KEPT PICTURE READS BACK AS THE LIVE ONE. `shot` streams the
  ;         capture through the same rotation map `p` streams the screen
  ;         through, so every logical pixel has to agree at every corner and
  ;         everywhere between. This is what makes one host decoder correct.
  y = 0
  While y < 8
    x = 0
    While x < 12
      live = ScrCapturePixel(#MON_FB_SCAN, 32, 90, 8, 12, x, y)
      kept = ScrCapturePixel(ScrShotPixels(), ScrShotField(#MON_SHOT_OFF_PITCH), ScrShotField(#MON_SHOT_OFF_ROT), ScrShotField(#MON_SHOT_OFF_PANELW), ScrShotField(#MON_SHOT_OFF_PANELH), x, y)
      If live <> kept : ProcedureReturn 40 : EndIf
      x = x + 1
    Wend
    y = y + 1
  Wend

  ; ---- 3. THE V3D TIER IS RECORDED AS ITSELF, and the frame is still the
  ;         one the panel scans: the GPU presents its finished physical
  ;         frame into the same buffer, so there is no second case here and
  ;         a tier that named the wrong path would make a measured frame
  ;         time unreadable.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_DSI
  gScrRot = 270
  gScrDsiUp = 1
  gDma = 1
  gV3dConOn = 1
  If ScrShotNow(#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 0) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 50 : EndIf
  rc = gate_header(12, 8, 32, 270, #HW_TIER_V3D, 0, 8, 12, #SCR_SRC_DSI, #MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 384, 2)
  If rc <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 60 + rc : EndIf
  If gate_copyIsScan(384) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 51 : EndIf

  ; THE SEQUENCE NUMBER ROSE. It is what tells a host "this picture is of
  ; the run I just asked for" from "this is the picture that was already
  ; here", and a stale capture is perfectly well formed.
  If ScrShotField(#MON_SHOT_OFF_SEQ) <> 2 : ProcedureReturn 52 : EndIf
  If ShotSeq() <> 2 : ProcedureReturn 53 : EndIf

  ; ---- 4. THE CPU TIER, straight through, at rotation 0 where the two
  ;         buffers are one.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_DSI
  gScrRot = 0
  gScrDsiUp = 1
  gDma = 0
  gV3dConOn = 0
  If ScrShotNow(#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 0) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 70 : EndIf
  rc = gate_header(8, 12, 32, 0, #HW_TIER_CPU, 0, 8, 12, #SCR_SRC_DSI, #MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 384, 3)
  If rc <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 80 + rc : EndIf

  ; ---- 5. THE OTHER SCREEN. An HDMI console's presented frame is the
  ;         firmware's view base and its own geometry, and the header says
  ;         so - a capture that recorded the panel's numbers on an HDMI run
  ;         would be decoded at the wrong pitch and look like a fault.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_HDMI
  gScrRot = 0
  gate_hdmiBase = #MON_FB_SCAN
  gate_hdmiW = 8
  gate_hdmiH = 12
  gate_hdmiPitch = 32
  gate_hdmiBpp = 4
  gDma = 1
  gV3dConOn = 0
  If ScrShotNow(#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 0) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 90 : EndIf
  rc = gate_header(8, 12, 32, 0, #HW_TIER_DMA, 0, 8, 12, #SCR_SRC_HDMI, #MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 384, 4)
  If rc <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 100 + rc : EndIf

  ; ---- 6. A REFUSED CAPTURE ON TOP OF A GOOD ONE. THE AREA IS NOT WIPED
  ;         FIRST, on purpose: this is the state the board is really in when
  ;         a run is captured and the next one is refused, and it is the one
  ;         state in which "the magic is cleared before anything is checked"
  ;         is the difference between no picture and the previous run's
  ;         picture presented as this run's.
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_NONE
  If ScrShotValid() <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 105 : EndIf
  If ScrShotNow(#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 0) <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 106 : EndIf
  If ScrShotValid() <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 107 : EndIf

  ; ---- 6b. And the same from a clean area, which is the first run's state.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_NONE
  If ScrShotNow(#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 0) <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 110 : EndIf
  If ScrShotValid() <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 111 : EndIf
  If ShotSeq() <> 4 : ProcedureReturn 112 : EndIf

  ; A DSI console whose panel is not scanning is the same answer.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_DSI
  gScrRot = 90
  gScrDsiUp = 0
  If ScrShotNow(#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 0) <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 113 : EndIf
  If ScrShotValid() <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 114 : EndIf

  ; ---- 7. A FRAME BIGGER THAN THE AREA IS REFUSED, not truncated. A short
  ;         capture decodes as a torn picture and reads as a display fault;
  ;         a refusal is a fact.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_HDMI
  gScrRot = 0
  gate_hdmiBase = #MON_FB_SCAN
  gate_hdmiW = 64
  gate_hdmiH = 32
  gate_hdmiPitch = 256
  gate_hdmiBpp = 4
  If ScrShotNow(#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 0) <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 120 : EndIf
  If ScrShotValid() <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 121 : EndIf

  ; ---- 8. THE PAYLOAD'S WAY BACK. The arm is set, the payload returns,
  ;         and the picture is kept BEFORE a single line is printed.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_DSI
  gScrRot = 90
  gScrDsiUp = 1
  gDma = 1
  gV3dConOn = 0
  gDead = 5
  gCacheOn = 1
  gate_payloadRc = 0
  ShotArm(1)
  If RunAt($00500000) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 130 : EndIf
  If gate_calls <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 131 : EndIf
  If ScrShotValid() <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 132 : EndIf
  ; THE ASSERTION THE WHOLE GATE IS FOR. At the FIRST character the monitor
  ; printed after the payload came back, the picture was already kept. On
  ; the board that first character is the repaint; a capture taken after it
  ; is a picture of the monitor's own report about the run.
  If gate_magicAtFirstPaint <> #MON_SHOT_MAGIC : ProcedureReturn 133 : EndIf
  If gate_paintsAfter = 0 : ProcedureReturn 143 : EndIf
  If gate_copyIsScan(384) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 134 : EndIf
  ; AND THE ARM IS SPENT. An arm that survived would overwrite this picture
  ; with the next run's, and the next run is the one nobody was watching.
  If ShotArmed() <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 135 : EndIf
  If ScrShotField(#MON_SHOT_OFF_WHO) <> #MON_SHOT_WHO_RETURN : ProcedureReturn 136 : EndIf
  ; The monitor's own recovery still happened, in the order it always did.
  If gate_ethReclaim <> 1 Or gate_cacheOn <> 1 Or gate_kbdResume <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 137 : EndIf
  If gate_wdStart <> 1 Or gate_wdStop <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 138 : EndIf
  ; THE DEADMAN IS SPENT BY THE PAYLOAD IT WAS ARMED FOR (forum 879).
  If gDead <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 146 : EndIf
  If gate_paints = 0 : ProcedureReturn 139 : EndIf
  ; The run record: entered once, before the jump; returned once, and before
  ; the picture was kept (a record written after the capture would be one
  ; more thing between the payload and the evidence).
  If gate_recEnter <> 1 Or gate_recReturn <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 144 : EndIf
  If gate_recOrder <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 145 : EndIf

  ; ---- 9. THE x0 IN THE HEADER IS THE x0 THE RUN ENDED WITH. A picture
  ;         and a return value that a host could pair up wrongly are worse
  ;         than either alone.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_DSI
  gScrRot = 90
  gScrDsiUp = 1
  gDma = 1
  gate_payloadRc = $65
  ShotArm(1)
  If RunAt($00500000) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 140 : EndIf
  If ScrShotField(#MON_SHOT_OFF_X0) <> $65 : ProcedureReturn 141 : EndIf
  If gGoRc <> $65 : ProcedureReturn 142 : EndIf

  ; ---- 10. UNARMED, NOTHING IS TAKEN. The capture is an instrument the
  ;          operator asks for; a monitor that captured every run would
  ;          spend a copy of the whole screen on every `run` and overwrite
  ;          whatever somebody was reading.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_DSI
  gScrRot = 90
  gScrDsiUp = 1
  gDma = 1
  gate_payloadRc = 0
  ShotArm(0)
  If RunAt($00500000) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 150 : EndIf
  If ScrShotValid() <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 151 : EndIf
  If ShotSeq() <> 6 : ProcedureReturn 152 : EndIf

  ; ---- 11. A JUMP INTO THE MONITOR IS STILL REFUSED, and refusing it must
  ;          not take a capture: nothing ran, so there is no frame to keep.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_DSI
  gScrRot = 90
  gScrDsiUp = 1
  ShotArm(1)
  gDead = 5
  gate_hitsAnswer = 1
  If RunAt($00300000) <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 160 : EndIf
  If gate_calls <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 161 : EndIf
  If ScrShotValid() <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 162 : EndIf
  ; THE ARM SURVIVES A REFUSAL. Nothing ran, so there is no frame to keep,
  ; and disarming here would mean an operator who mistyped an address had to
  ; remember to arm again - which is exactly how a run comes back with no
  ; picture and nobody can say why.
  If ShotArmed() <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 163 : EndIf
  ; A refused jump writes no run record, so the run number does not move and
  ; a host can tell "never entered" from every other ending.
  If gate_recEnter <> 0 Or gate_recReturn <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 164 : EndIf
  ; And a refused jump does not spend a deadman either.
  If gDead <> 5 : ProcedureReturn 165 : EndIf
  ShotArm(0)

  ; A quarantined DMA writer blocks screenshot memory access even when
  ; acceleration preference is off. Execute the real DisplayMemorySafe.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_DSI
  gScrRot = 90
  gScrDsiUp = 1
  gDma = 0
  gate_quarantined = 1
  If ScrShotNow(#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 0) <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 170 : EndIf
  If ScrShotValid() <> 0 : ProcedureReturn 171 : EndIf
  gate_quarantined = 0

  ; ---- 12. THE NUMBER SURVIVES A RESET (forum 876). The capture area is
  ;          DRAM and outlives a reset; the counter is BSS and does not. So
  ;          model the first capture of a fresh boot: an area that already
  ;          holds picture 41 and a counter back at zero. The new picture
  ;          must be 42, or a host rightly refuses it as the old one.
  gate_fresh()
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_DSI
  gScrRot = 90
  gScrDsiUp = 1
  gDma = 1
  PokeI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_SEQ, 41)
  PokeI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_MAGIC, #MON_SHOT_MAGIC)
  gShotSeq = 0
  If ScrShotNow(#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 0) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 180 : EndIf
  If ScrShotField(#MON_SHOT_OFF_SEQ) <> 42 : ProcedureReturn 181 : EndIf
  ; And a torn or absent header cannot drag the count anywhere.
  gate_fresh()
  PokeI(#MON_SHOT_HDR + #MON_SHOT_OFF_SEQ, 900)
  gScrSrc = #SCR_SRC_DSI
  gScrRot = 90
  gScrDsiUp = 1
  If ScrShotNow(#MON_SHOT_WHO_PAYLOAD, 0) <> 1 : ProcedureReturn 182 : EndIf
  If ScrShotField(#MON_SHOT_OFF_SEQ) <> 43 : ProcedureReturn 183 : EndIf

  PokeI(#GATE_OUT, gate_paints)
  PokeI(#GATE_OUT + 8, ShotSeq())
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure

Main()
